# cuts/v1.0.46/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# WHY v1.0.46 EXISTS: v1.0.45 shipped a daemon that could not contain the thing
# the cut was for. hub-v0.4.64 was built from oa c4c5b40b408e -- the SAME commit
# v1.0.45 pinned -- and published at 05:30:04Z, while the cost panel (oa #346)
# merged at 10:56:11Z. Measured with `git merge-base --is-ancestor` rather than
# read off a board row: oa #340 and #341 ARE in 0.4.64 (the nav-crop fix and
# advanced-settings genuinely shipped); #345, #346 and #347 are NOT.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 DAEMON_COMMIT NAMES THE ARTEFACT, NOT THE TREE. DO NOT "UPDATE" IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hub-v0.4.65 is built, Developer ID signed, notarised, stapled and PUBLISHED.
# It was compiled from ostler-assistant 4d1f47ae. That is a fact about a binary
# that already exists on a release, and it does not change when oa main moves.
#
# So if a later reader finds oa main ahead of 4d1f47ae, the correct response is
# NOT to advance this line -- it is to ask whether the daemon must be REBUILT.
# The artefact is the fact; the tree is the claim; when they disagree, change
# the claim. Editing this line to match a tree is how a cut acquires false
# provenance, which is the v1.0.14 failure.
#
# oa PR #349 (the hub-app build-info emitter) is DELIBERATELY NOT MERGED before
# this cut, so oa main stays at 4d1f47ae and the daemon row stays FRESH rather
# than HELD. Discriminator run before deciding, not assumed: does anything in
# the v1.0.46 pipeline consume the emitter FROM THE TREE, e.g. a gate that
# re-derives the sidecar instead of reading the published one?
#   CM051 origin/main  grep -l 'emit-build-info|emit-hub-build-info' -> 0 files
#   OS003 origin/main  same predicate                                -> 0 files
#   CONTROL, same repos, 'build-info'                -> 18 and 5 files
# So the predicate is live and the zero is real absence. Both consumers I read
# (scripts/verify_cut_freshness.sh, scripts/verify_cut_manifest.py) FETCH the
# published release asset over the API. Nothing re-derives. #349 lands after
# the tag, in v1.0.47.
#
# ARTEFACTS, verified against the SERVER rather than against what was uploaded
# (daemon re-downloaded from the release and re-hashed):
#   ostler-releases   hub-v0.4.65  ostler-assistant-...-v0.4.65.tar.gz  8222931f
#                     TeamIdentifier=V95N2B8X7A, source=Notarized Developer ID,
#                     stapler rc=0
#   ostler-assistant  hub-v0.4.65  ostler-hub-app-...-v0.4.65.tar.gz    9f77ab15
#                     Signature=adhoc, TeamIdentifier=not set -- CORRECT, adhoc
#                     BY DESIGN, the DMG carries the outer seal
# Both build-info.json files report 4d1f47ae, and for the Hub app that value was
# PROBED out of the Mach-O inside the shipped tarball, not copied from a build
# log (HR015 #225/#732).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 names the tree whose install.sh SHIPS, compared by BLOB IDENTITY and not
# by ancestry. 359ea636 is main immediately after CM051 #1046 merged. The PR
# that adds this file touches cuts/ ONLY -- not install.sh, not gui/Makefile --
# so the blob it names is the blob that ships.
#
# 🔴 A DAEMON BUMP TOUCHES FOUR PIN SITES, AND TWO OF THEM ARE DIGESTS.
# Verified on origin/main AFTER the merge, not from the PR diff:
#   gui/Makefile  DAEMON_VERSION      0.4.65
#   gui/Makefile  DAEMON_SHA256       8222931f...  (the ostler-releases copy)
#   gui/Makefile  HUB_APP_SHA256      9f77ab15...  (the ostler-assistant copy)
#   install.sh    OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION          0.4.65
#   install.sh    DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256  8222931f...
# The first pass moved only the two VERSION sites, because the sweep was keyed
# on the string "0.4.64" and a SHA-256 does not contain its version number. A
# search that cannot express the thing it is looking for returns a confident
# partial answer. tests/test_daemon_pins_agree.sh caught it: 10 passed / 0
# failed after the fix, and locally that run is STRICTLY STRONGER than CI's,
# because on the runner site 6 reports "[skip] could not reach hub-v0.4.65 in
# ostler-assistant (auth/offline). NOT a pass" for want of an ostler-ai token.
# Sweep for the OUTGOING DIGEST as well as the outgoing version.
#
# ASSISTANT_FALLBACK_VERSION stays at 0.4.62 deliberately. It is the
# last-known-good retry target, not a mirror of the pin; moving it in lockstep
# would leave a bad primary pin with nothing older to fall back to.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VENDOR ROWS: TWO GRAFTS AND AN ACK, NOT A WAVE-THROUGH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# verify_cut_freshness.sh refused this cut at RC=1 "DO NOT CUT" on two vendor
# rows, from three HR015 commits that landed 2026-08-25 AFTER v1.0.45 was cut.
# Adjudicated per file against the SHIPPED tree, with a control proving the
# probe can see (vendor/ostler_fda/extract_all.py PRESENT):
#   #694 13754987  identifier_quality.py    VENDORED -> GRAFTED
#   #698 975a8de8  apple_mail_mbox.py       VENDORED -> GRAFTED
#   #695 accbc425  test_whatsapp_pair.py    ABSENT   -> hold_ack
# Pins HELD, not advanced: advancing ostler_fda means regenerating its
# divergence patch, and regenerate_forbidden_reason records that the export
# carries real person-name tokens out of a private repo into a public one.
# Gate re-run after: RC=0, stale/RED=0, fresh=17 held=5 exempt=5 cannot-verify=0.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Board #844: a green cut repoints ostler.ai/install.dmg automatically, and all
# twelve box-walk probes SKIP. Nothing between "gates green" and "customer
# download" is a runtime proof. Recording that here so the next reader does not
# mistake a green gate set for a walked build.
#
# 🔴 OFFLINE STAPLING IS NOT PROVEN AND BELONGS IN THE BOX WALK. `stapler` said
# "Downloaded ticket has been stored at..." -- that is a ticket RESOLVED OVER
# THE NETWORK, not proof of a locally stapled one. Board #221 was exactly this:
# Ostler.app shipped without its ticket and broke offline first-run. Walk test:
# pull the network, launch, watch Gatekeeper. Nobody may claim "offline install
# unaffected" until that has been done.
CUT_VERSION=1.0.46
DAEMON_COMMIT=4d1f47ae
CM051=359ea636f67c6284024b67d919fcdd9111369c02
